message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "pyobfus: An AST-based Python obfuscator with reverse stack-trace mapping for AI-assisted development"
abstract: >-
  pyobfus is an open-source, source-to-source obfuscator for Python built on the
  standard-library abstract syntax tree (ast). It renames identifiers, encodes
  string and numeric literals, and rewrites imports consistently across a
  multi-file project, emitting ordinary .py files that run on CPython 3.9-3.14
  without a native runtime or bytecode VM. Its distinguishing feature is a
  reverse mapping workflow that translates an obfuscated production stack trace
  back to the original names, so a developer or an AI coding assistant can debug
  shipped code without weakening protection. The same operations are exposed
  through a JSON command-line interface and a Model Context Protocol server.
